Z||000000||Devotshka||11-24-2001||09:44 PM||||Anyone have any brand preferences or good/bad experiences to share?  I need to get one but don't know if there are some i should maybe stay away from, etc.  Not too keen on buying consumable things from ebay either  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Thanks!||||reg||5
Z||000001||fierospeeder||11-24-2001||10:38 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.jcwhitney.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.jcwhitney.com</A>  has some <P>i would also look in some 4X4, offroading magazines for some ads.<P>If i see any ill post some.  A lot of offroading people use it for better starting, on board welders etc...<P>------------------<BR>Fiero Technician<P>74 Vw Beetle<BR>83 Honda Nighthawk 550<BR>84 Pontiac Fiero<BR>87 Ford Thunderbird Turbo<P>Selling a car is like giving your own kid for adoption.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Nashco||11-24-2001||10:48 PM||||Are you talking battery isolators like...having one battery do all the work for X stuff, another battery dedicated for Y stuff, but the same charging source?<P>If so, the best place to go is an RV shop, they'll hook you up with something that is made to be used a lot and will hold up reliably.  They'll also have a good range if you're cheap or if you want something of high quality.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||FormulaJoe||11-25-2001||10:20 AM||||Boat shops too.  I remember when I was into 4X4 and offroading, saw an article about battery switches and isolators in an offroad mag.  Went to a boat shop and they had several of the items mentioned.  The offroad mags are a good resource they have tons of advertisers in the back for all sorts of things.  Might try your local library too, some have subscriptions to magazines and have them bound every year.  You can go in and look up an article in an index and pull out that issue and photo copy it.<P>------------------<BR>Yellow Formula<BR>(soon to be 3.4 DOHC)||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||11-25-2001||11:00 AM||||I put a battery isolator on mine a couple weeks ago when i got stuck with a dead battery. It just goes where the pos+ cable does. shuts off battery power to car if it drops below 11 volts. All I have to do is push a button and it reconnects. Is that the kind your talking about? Only uses the original (1) battery.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Devotshka||11-25-2001||01:30 PM||||Thanks for the tips guys.  I'm going to check out the local RV place this week... probably just for suggestions too though, i'm sure their prices will be 2X retail  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>The isolator is going to be used for hooking two batteries up in parallel.  In the future i plan on switching duties with them, so the stereo system (read: battery killer) has its own juice.  Thanks for the info!<BR>||||reg||1
